From 65e32157da6f512f6fa1a4a5d82670d6114573d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:46:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-model priority-shaped concurrency limit

Requests carrying a JSON "priority" field (lower is more urgent, as vLLM's
--scheduling-policy priority reads it) are now admitted by a prefix test: a
request at priority p gets in when fewer than priorityConcurrencyLimit
requests are in flight at priority <= p. A flood of low-urgency traffic can no
longer shed an urgent request. One priority level can still fill the whole cap,
so total in flight can exceed it.

Opt-in per model via the new priorityConcurrencyLimit key. Unset or 0 leaves a
model on the flat concurrencyLimit test, byte-for-byte as before; when both
keys are set the new one wins. Rejection is the same 429 with Retry-After: 1.
The field is the request body's, unrelated to
routing.scheduler.settings.fifo.priority, which ranks queued swaps and is
higher-is-first.

Admission bookkeeping becomes one ledger per model, keyed by priority with
buckets in ascending order, so the model's total is the sum of its buckets
rather than a second counter that could fall out of step. Every release site
carries the priority the admitting HandlerReq held (or the ServeDoneEvent
built from it), and a release that finds no such bucket panics naming the
model and priority.
